# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: x86_64 | v0.18 | aws/ubuntu2604
# Enterprise Linux Audit Policy v0.18 | aws/ubuntu2604 | Tier 2 — targeted shell-startup watches active; broad /etc proposal remains inactive
# Source: enterprise SOC/IR; Unix shell vendor documentation and audited installed path prerequisites.
# These watch system-level startup file changes (writes and attributes only), not user home dotfiles or reads.
# /etc/profile and the distro Bash startup file are standard installed-package paths, but must resolve on the selected image.
# Do not claim auditd file-path watches detect creation of previously absent single files.
# Objective: persistent/system security config changes irrespective of CVE association.
# /etc generally exists, but individual security configuration files may not.
# The proposed directory rule would cover creation and modification under /etc,
# including loader settings, system shell profiles, SSH and sudoers if present.
# Not enabled by default: broad /etc collection needs tier-2 promotion approval,
# duplicate/overlap review and volume justification for busy and cloud hosts.
# Audits writes/attribute changes, NOT file reads; covers both ABI variants.
# # -a always,exit -F dir=/etc -F perm=wa -k t2_etc_integrity


# v0.17 ACTIVE: CVE-independent system-wide shell startup integrity.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F path=/etc/profile -F perm=wa -k t2_shell_init
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -F path=/etc/profile -F perm=wa -k t2_shell_init
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F path=/etc/bash.bashrc -F perm=wa -k t2_shell_init
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -F path=/etc/bash.bashrc -F perm=wa -k t2_shell_init
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/profile.d -F perm=wa -k t2_shell_init
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -F dir=/etc/profile.d -F perm=wa -k t2_shell_init
# These rule keys are distinct from STIG watches; do not duplicate existing profile rules in other files.
# /etc/profile.d is a documented default family directory; customized/minimal images still need a path preflight.

# CVE-independent Magic SysRq control; conditional to kernel/sysctl support.
# No general unfiltered /etc audit rule: cloud profiles may already have a scoped auid=unset/euid=0 /etc rule; sysctl procfs actions require independent, applicable telemetry.
# These procfs candidates require kernel/filesystem-specific audit acceptance checks; remain inactive:
# -a always,exit -F path=/proc/sysrq-trigger -F perm=w -k t2_sysrq
# -a always,exit -F path=/proc/sys/kernel/sysrq -F perm=wa -k t2_sysrq

# Narrow leaf-path alternative, usable only when the file already exists:
# -a always,exit -F path=/etc/ld.so.preload -F perm=wa -k t2_loader_preload
# This leaf watch cannot monitor initial creation when the file is absent.
# Prefer filtered Sysmon-for-Linux FileCreate / EDR file telemetry for initial creation.
# Unfiltered /etc and loader leaf candidates remain inactive; cloud-only scoped /etc rules are separate.

